 "text": "Hi, how are you holding up? Totally normal feeling. Want act like you've been there a million times anyway. What's your favorite food? Go with classic that suits your taste. Pasta, a bird, a salad. Stick to basics and you can always try something flashy if you like the place. Dress as if you' going for an interview. A smart shirt, a clean dress, and simple accessories. Ask the waitstaff to help. Most people do little bits of help, so it feels like being served by a team. Yes, it's a great way to try something new without feeling committed. Pick one item and ask how it pairs with the basic dish.",
